## 5. Protocol Portability: Schemas Are Not Permissions

Exposing raw OpenAPI endpoints or Model Context Protocol (`MCP`) tools directly to an LLM treats transport schemas as security boundaries. In a governed control plane, every external operation is compiled into an immutable **Canonical Capability Contract** with pinned SHA-256 digests (`connectorContractHash`) and automatic quarantine when upstream tool definitions change:

{% canonicalcontract /%}

---

## 6. Proportional Risk Governance (`R0`–`R4`) Over Binary Prompts

Asking a user to click *"Confirm"* on every tool call creates approval fatigue on low-risk actions while confusing **user confirmation** with **institutional authorization** on high-risk actions. Inspect the five risk tiers (`R0`–`R4`) and test the dynamic escalation rules below:

